// EXPECT: PASS
// Over-rejection guard for the higher-order forwarded-argument fix. The closure params are bound to
// a conservative JOIN over the call's other arguments, so a call whose arguments are all CLEAN must
// stay clean. If this goes red, the join is charging on the mere presence of a closure argument
// rather than on what the sibling arguments actually carry, and the fix has become a wall.
fn apply(f, v) { f(v); }
fn main() {
    let k = 42;
    apply(|v| { print(v); }, k);
}
